new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8160c3d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/DEVICE-SETTINGS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+# AsusSMC device settings — ASUS Control 1.1.4
+
+Based on `hieplpvip/AsusSMC` commit
+`c15d2f297c86b65a3cb866cc2bcece595c136417`. Original MIT licensing and notices
+remain. The kext keeps its upstream `com.hieplpvip.AsusSMC` identifier,
+`AsusSMC` service class and `AsusSMC.kext` filename. ASUS Control is the
+separate preference pane and optional user-session policy agent.
+
+## Hardware profiles and build
+
+The software interfaces use generic ASUS Control names. Endpoint addresses
+and model restrictions are isolated in `AsusSMC/Models/X1605VA305.hpp`.
+Only ASUS X1605VA BIOS 305 is currently profiled. A similarly wired device
+still requires validation; the product name does not imply compatibility.
+
+```sh
+bash build-device-settings.sh
+```
+
+Command Line Tools build using MacKernelSDK
+`3f750085caa17ec3a7880f11c11bf4f48cd6a164`, Lilu 1.7.2 and VirtualSMC 1.3.8
+SDK headers. Output: `build-device-settings/AsusSMC.kext`. Build runs decoder,
+command-boundary, startup-contract and signature checks. It never installs or
+loads the result. The module version remains upstream1.4.1, read from the
+Xcode project; ASUS Control1.1.4 has separate userspace versioning. Settings
+API2 / feature revision3 identify the added functions.
+
+The known firmware wiring is detected from cached DSDT signatures. No
+fan/settings boot arguments are required. Only the known X1605VA BIOS305
+wiring is validated. No SMBIOS model check, new ACPI startup query or arbitrary
+EC register interface is added. Preserve the existing percentage-backlight
+SSDT and Lilu/VirtualSMC load order. No new SSDT is needed.
+
+## Boot boundary
+
+The user corrected the earlier attribution: the boot stall was unrelated to
+AsusSMC. This extended build wakes the existing timer for accepted userspace
+commands. Older custom API2 drivers remain compatible with the pane, but retain
+their original feature gates and dispatch latency.
+
+Only the previously implemented fan-monitoring path runs automatically. Added
+settings discovery and queries require an explicit queued userspace request.
+The profile also suppresses upstream's automatic 80% battery-limit write at
+startup; battery writes require an explicit command. No new setting is written
+by this kext at login or wake. The optional policy agent runs after user login
+and only when configured by the pane.
+
+## Queue and compatibility
+
+All added firmware operations run on the existing sensor workloop. The
+property handler validates privilege, exact dictionary shape, value bounds
+and a nonzero uint32 request ID, then enqueues one request. It never evaluates
+ACPI. A single pending slot serializes fan, keyboard, readback and device
+operations. Cache properties are consumed by userspace.
+
+- Legacy fan: exactly `FanCommand` + `FanRequestID`. Commands 1 Auto, 2 Full
+  Speed, 3 Standard, 4 Whisper, 5 Performance. Administrator-only, on recognized firmware.
+- Keyboard: exactly `KeyboardPercent` (0–100) + `KeyboardRequestID`.
+  Local-console user or administrator; discovered `GKPC`/`SKPC` required.
+- Readback: exactly `SettingsCommand=1` + `SettingsRequestID`. Local-console
+  user or administrator; discovers keyboard methods lazily and refreshes
+  profile, keyboard, battery capability, Fn mode and touchpad state.
+- Device: exactly `DeviceCommand` + `DeviceRequestID`. Local-console user or
+  administrator, on recognized firmware, API2. Values below.
+
+| Device command | Request |
+| --- | --- |
+| 1 / 2 | Charge limit 80% / 100% |
+| 3 / 4 | Printed hotkeys / F1–F12 as primary keys |
+| 5 / 6 | Enable / disable built-in touchpad |
+| 7 / 8 / 9 | Auto fan policy, then Standard / Whisper / Performance |
+| 10 / 11 | Full Speed / Automatic fan policy |
+
+Each family publishes its own `…CommandSucceeded` and
+`…CompletedRequestID`, with completion ID written last. Legacy fan also
+retains `FanCommandReply`. Firmware reply 1 acknowledges a request; it does
+not establish physical behavior. Touchpad IANE notification is asynchronous;
+userspace confirms subsequent driver readback. A timeout cannot cancel a
+firmware call. Do not resubmit accepted requests automatically.
+
+`AsusControlAPIVersion=2` and `AsusControlHardwareProfile` describe the current
+interface/profile. `X1605VA-ControlAPIVersion=1` and old diagnostic aliases
+remain solely for compatibility. Added controls publish capability and validity
+flags; absent/invalid data must not be interpreted as zero or enabled.
+
+## Current firmware wiring
+
+- Fan DSTS `0x00110013`: reject `FFFFFFFE`/`FFFFFFFF`, require presence, low16
+  ×100 RPM. Reject fpe2 overflow. Stopped fan is valid. DEVS 0 Auto / 1 Full.
+- Thermal DSTS/DEVS `0x00110019`: Standard0, Whisper1, Performance2. No ROG
+  policy or arbitrary fan curve is assumed. Fan mode is last acknowledged
+  request, not an independent mode sensor.
+- Charge limit DEVS `0x00120057`: only 80 or100. DSTS provides capability
+  flags, **not numeric charge-limit readback**. `ChargeLimitRequested` is an
+  acknowledgement cache, not proof of charging enforcement. User observed
+  charging above80%; resending on source/session changes needs physical testing.
+  The24-hour full-charge timer lives in userspace.
+- Fn lock `0x00100023`: accept only exact DSTS `0x10000` or `0x10001`; DEVS
+  0 normal / 1 hotkeys. Other return patterns remain unavailable.
+- Keyboard `GKPC`/`SKPC` from existing SSDT; 0–100 cache, not measured light.
+- Touchpad: typed Boolean GetTouchStatus message to exactly one whitelisted
+  VoodooI2C touchpad service; writes replay ATKD `IANE(0x6B)`, the existing
+  Fn+F6 notification. Touchscreens and external mice are not selected.
+
+User-space policy restricts Performance to AC + battery >40% and Full Speed to
+AC on this profile. The agent falls back to Standard when Performance becomes
+ineligible and restores Performance on eligible AC. It also handles charge
+deadlines and keyboard idle restore. No profile-switching UI or LPM rules.
+No microphone, screen-brightness or key remapping is added here.
+
+## Validation limits
+
+Earlier fan-only patches physically verified RPM and Auto/Full Speed on BIOS
+305 (including stopped and approximately 5700–5800 RPM full-speed observations).
+These are not calibrated manufacturer min/max limits. Thermal profile requests
+received firmware acknowledgements. New settings need a deliberate hardware
+test. Compilation, fixtures and static startup checks do not prove boot,
+sleep/wake or physical device control.
diff --git a/Tests/boot-contract.py b/Tests/boot-contract.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..05b1d1f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Tests/boot-contract.py
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+"""Guard the specific boot-path regression boundary; no driver is loaded."""
+from pathlib import Path
+
+source = Path('AsusSMC/AsusSMC.cpp').read_text()
+startup = source.split('bool AsusSMC::start(', 1)[1].split('void AsusSMC::stop(', 1)[0]
+callback = source.split('bool AsusSMC::vsmcNotificationHandler(', 1)[1].split('EXPORT extern', 1)[0]
+for name, body in [('start', startup), ('sensor callback', callback)]:
+    for forbidden in ['initKeyboardDevice(', 'refreshDeviceSettings(', 'evaluateInteger("GKPC"', 'evaluateInteger("SKPC"']:
+        assert forbidden not in body, f'{name} performs unsolicited settings work: {forbidden}'
+process = source.split('void AsusSMC::processFanCommand()', 1)[1].split('void AsusSMC::initKeyboardDevice()', 1)[0]
+assert 'if (cmd == 0x200U)' in process and 'refreshDeviceSettings();' in process
+print('PASS: no new settings discovery/queries in startup or periodic callback; explicit queued refresh required.')
+
+handler = source.split('IOReturn AsusSMC::setProperties(', 1)[1].split('void AsusSMC::processFanCommand()', 1)[0]
+assert 'poller->setTimeoutMS(0)' in handler
+assert 'evaluateInteger(' not in handler and 'wmi_evaluate_method(' not in handler
+print('PASS: accepted commands wake the workloop; the property handler performs no firmware calls.')
+
+for argument in ['-asusctrl', 'asusctrlprofile', '-x1605vafan']:
+    assert argument not in startup, f'Custom boot argument still required: {argument}'
+assert 'getACPITableData("DSDT")' in startup and 'matchesFirmware(' in startup
+assert 'MODULE_VERSION = 1.4.1;' in Path('AsusSMC.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj').read_text()
+print('PASS: cached-table automatic matching, no control boot-argument gates, upstream version retained.')
diff --git a/Tests/protocol.cpp b/Tests/protocol.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..91f982e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Tests/protocol.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+#include "../AsusSMC/AsusControlProtocol.hpp"
+#include <cassert>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <vector>
+#include <fstream>
+#include "../AsusSMC/Models/X1605VA305.hpp"
+int main(int argc, char **argv) {
+    uint16_t rpm = 1234;
+    assert(!AsusControl::decodeRPM(0xfffffffeU, rpm) && rpm == 1234);
+    assert(!AsusControl::decodeRPM(0xffffffffU, rpm));
+    assert(!AsusControl::decodeRPM(0, rpm));
+    assert(AsusControl::decodeRPM(0x10000, rpm) && rpm == 0);
+    assert(AsusControl::decodeRPM(0x1000f, rpm) && rpm == 1500);
+    assert(AsusControl::decodeRPM(0x1003a, rpm) && rpm == 5800);
+    assert(AsusControl::decodeRPM(0x100a3, rpm) && rpm == 16300);
+    assert(!AsusControl::decodeRPM(0x100a4, rpm) && rpm == 16300);
+    uint32_t profile = 99;
+    for (uint32_t value = 0; value < 3; ++value)
+        assert(AsusControl::decodeProfile(0x03030000U | value, profile) && profile == value);
+    assert(!AsusControl::decodeProfile(0xfffffffeU, profile));
+    assert(!AsusControl::decodeProfile(0x03030003U, profile));
+    assert(!AsusControl::decodeProfile(1, profile));
+    bool hotkeys = false;
+    assert(AsusControl::decodeFnLock(0x10001, hotkeys) && hotkeys);
+    assert(AsusControl::decodeFnLock(0x10000, hotkeys) && !hotkeys);
+    assert(!AsusControl::decodeFnLock(0xfffffffe, hotkeys));
+    assert(!AsusControl::decodeFnLock(0x10201, hotkeys));
+    assert(!AsusControl::devicePresent(0xfffffffe));
+    assert(AsusControl::devicePresent(0x00990200));
+    assert(!AsusControl::validDeviceCommand(0));
+    assert(AsusControl::validDeviceCommand(1) && AsusControl::validDeviceCommand(11));
+    assert(!AsusControl::validDeviceCommand(12));
+    std::vector<uint8_t> table(36,0);
+    const char signature[]="DSDT",oem[]="_ASUS_";
+    for(unsigned i=0;i<4;++i)table[i]=signature[i];
+    for(unsigned i=0;i<6;++i)table[10+i]=oem[i];
+    table.insert(table.end(),AsusControl::FanReadWiring,AsusControl::FanReadWiring+sizeof(AsusControl::FanReadWiring));
+    table.insert(table.end(),AsusControl::ThermalWriteWiring,AsusControl::ThermalWriteWiring+sizeof(AsusControl::ThermalWriteWiring));
+    table.insert(table.end(),AsusControl::FnReadWiring,AsusControl::FnReadWiring+sizeof(AsusControl::FnReadWiring));
+    for(unsigned i=0;i<4;++i)table[4+i]=(table.size()>>(8*i))&0xff;
+    assert(AsusControl::matchesFirmware(table.data(),table.size()));
+    table[10]='X';assert(!AsusControl::matchesFirmware(table.data(),table.size()));table[10]='_';
+    table.back()^=1;assert(!AsusControl::matchesFirmware(table.data(),table.size()));
+    assert(!AsusControl::matchesFirmware(table.data(),20));
+    if(argc==2) {
+        std::ifstream file(argv[1],std::ios::binary);
+        std::vector<uint8_t> real((std::istreambuf_iterator<char>(file)),{});
+        assert(AsusControl::matchesFirmware(real.data(),real.size()));
+        puts("PASS: known local firmware matches without boot arguments.");
+    }
+    puts("PASS: RPM decoding, stopped fan, fpe2 limits, unsupported sentinels, and Vivobook profiles.");
+}
diff --git a/build-device-settings.sh b/build-device-settings.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5ffecf1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build-device-settings.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+#!/bin/bash
+set -euo pipefail
+cd "$(dirname "$0")"
+TASK_ROOT="$PWD"
+RELEASE_VERSION=$(python3 - <<'PYSOURCE'
+import pathlib,re
+values=set(re.findall(r'MODULE_VERSION = ([0-9.]+);',pathlib.Path('AsusSMC.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj').read_text()))
+assert len(values)==1
+print(values.pop())
+PYSOURCE
+)
+[[ "$RELEASE_VERSION" =~ ^[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$ ]] || { echo "Invalid VERSION" >&2; exit 1; }
+BUILD_DIR="$TASK_ROOT/build-device-settings"
+DEPS_DIR="${ASUS_CONTROL_DEPS:-${X1605VA_DEPS:-$TASK_ROOT/.deps}}"
+mkdir -p "$DEPS_DIR" "$BUILD_DIR/obj" "$BUILD_DIR/AsusSMC.kext/Contents/MacOS"
+if [[ ! -d "$DEPS_DIR/MacKernelSDK/Headers" ]]; then
+  curl --fail --location --silent --show-error https://github.com/acidanthera/MacKernelSDK/archive/3f750085caa17ec3a7880f11c11bf4f48cd6a164.tar.gz -o "$DEPS_DIR/sdk.tar.gz"
+  tar -xzf "$DEPS_DIR/sdk.tar.gz" -C "$DEPS_DIR"
+  mv "$DEPS_DIR/MacKernelSDK-3f750085caa17ec3a7880f11c11bf4f48cd6a164" "$DEPS_DIR/MacKernelSDK"
+fi
+if [[ ! -d "$DEPS_DIR/Lilu.kext/Contents/Resources/Headers" ]]; then
+  curl --fail --location --silent --show-error https://github.com/acidanthera/Lilu/releases/download/1.7.2/Lilu-1.7.2-DEBUG.zip -o "$DEPS_DIR/lilu.zip"
+  mkdir -p "$DEPS_DIR/lilu-download"
+  ditto -x -k "$DEPS_DIR/lilu.zip" "$DEPS_DIR/lilu-download"
+  ditto "$DEPS_DIR/lilu-download/Lilu.kext" "$DEPS_DIR/Lilu.kext"
+fi
+if [[ ! -f "$DEPS_DIR/VirtualSMC.kext/Contents/Resources/VirtualSMCSDK/kern_vsmcapi.hpp" ]]; then
+  curl --fail --location --silent --show-error https://github.com/acidanthera/VirtualSMC/releases/download/1.3.8/VirtualSMC-1.3.8-DEBUG.zip -o "$DEPS_DIR/vsmc.zip"
+  mkdir -p "$DEPS_DIR/vsmc-download"
+  ditto -x -k "$DEPS_DIR/vsmc.zip" "$DEPS_DIR/vsmc-download"
+  ditto "$DEPS_DIR/vsmc-download/Kexts/VirtualSMC.kext" "$DEPS_DIR/VirtualSMC.kext"
+fi
+FLAGS=(-arch x86_64 -mmacosx-version-min=11.0 -mkernel -nostdinc -fno-builtin -fno-common -fno-stack-protector
+  -DKERNEL -DKERNEL_PRIVATE -DDRIVER_PRIVATE -DAPPLE -DNeXT -DPRODUCT_NAME=AsusSMC "-DMODULE_VERSION=$RELEASE_VERSION"
+  -isystem "$(xcrun clang -print-resource-dir)/include" -I"$DEPS_DIR/MacKernelSDK/Headers"
+  -I"$DEPS_DIR/Lilu.kext/Contents/Resources" -I"$DEPS_DIR/VirtualSMC.kext/Contents/Resources"
+  -IAsusSMC -IGlobal -IKernEventServer -IVirtualAppleKeyboard -Os -Wall -Wextra
+  -Wno-unused-parameter -Wno-inconsistent-missing-override)
+for SOURCE in AsusSMC/AsusSMC.cpp AsusSMC/KeyImplementations.cpp VirtualAppleKeyboard/VirtualAppleKeyboard.cpp KernEventServer/KernEventServer.cpp; do
+  xcrun clang++ "${FLAGS[@]}" -fapple-kext -std=gnu++14 -nostdinc++ -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti -fno-use-cxa-atexit -fno-threadsafe-statics \
+    -c "$SOURCE" -o "$BUILD_DIR/obj/$(basename "${SOURCE%.cpp}").o"
+done
+cat > "$BUILD_DIR/kmod_info.c" <<CEND
+#include <mach/mach_types.h>
+extern kern_return_t AsusSMC_kern_start(kmod_info_t *, void *);
+extern kern_return_t AsusSMC_kern_stop(kmod_info_t *, void *);
+KMOD_EXPLICIT_DECL(com.hieplpvip.AsusSMC, "$RELEASE_VERSION", AsusSMC_kern_start, AsusSMC_kern_stop)
+__private_extern__ kmod_start_func_t *_realmain = 0;
+__private_extern__ kmod_stop_func_t *_antimain = 0;
+__private_extern__ int _kext_apple_cc = __APPLE_CC__;
+CEND
+xcrun clang "${FLAGS[@]}" -c "$BUILD_DIR/kmod_info.c" -o "$BUILD_DIR/obj/kmod_info.o"
+xcrun clang++ -arch x86_64 -mmacosx-version-min=11.0 -nostdlib -Xlinker -kext -Xlinker -export_dynamic \
+  "$BUILD_DIR"/obj/*.o -L"$DEPS_DIR/MacKernelSDK/Library/x86_64" -lkmodc++ -lkmod -lcc_kext \
+  -o "$BUILD_DIR/AsusSMC.kext/Contents/MacOS/AsusSMC"
+python3 - "$RELEASE_VERSION" "$BUILD_DIR" <<'PY'
+import pathlib, plistlib, sys
+version, target = sys.argv[1:]
+values = {'$(DEVELOPMENT_LANGUAGE)':'en', '$(EXECUTABLE_NAME)':'AsusSMC',
+    '$(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER)':'com.hieplpvip.AsusSMC', '$(PRODUCT_NAME)':'AsusSMC', '$(MODULE_VERSION)':version}
+def expand(item):
+    if isinstance(item, dict): return {k:expand(v) for k,v in item.items()}
+    if isinstance(item, list): return [expand(v) for v in item]
+    if isinstance(item, str):
+        for key, value in values.items(): item = item.replace(key, value)
+    return item
+info = expand(plistlib.loads(pathlib.Path('AsusSMC/Info.plist').read_bytes()))
+pathlib.Path(target, 'AsusSMC.kext/Contents/Info.plist').write_bytes(plistlib.dumps(info, sort_keys=False))
+PY
+xcrun clang++ -std=c++14 -Wall -Wextra -Werror Tests/protocol.cpp -o "$BUILD_DIR/protocol-test"
+"$BUILD_DIR/protocol-test"
+python3 Tests/boot-contract.py
+codesign --force --sign - "$BUILD_DIR/AsusSMC.kext"
+codesign --verify --strict "$BUILD_DIR/AsusSMC.kext"
+echo "Built AsusSMC $RELEASE_VERSION in $BUILD_DIR. Nothing was installed or loaded."
